    >>> jnp.convolve(x1, y1, mode='full')
    Array([ 4., 13., 26., 31., 26., 13.,  4.], dtype=float32)

    For complex-valued inputs:

    >>> x2 = jnp.array([3+1j, 2, 2-3j])
    >>> y2 = jnp.array([4, 2-5j, 1])
    >>> jnp.correlate(x2, y2, mode='full')
